WEBVTT

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:04.762
 بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيم اَلْحَمْدُ لِلَّٰهِ وَالصَّلاةُ وَالسَّلامُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللهِ

00:00:04.786 --> 00:00:06.786
وَعَلَى آلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ اَجْمَعِينَ

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:07.560
 اَمَّا بَعْدُ

00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:10.380
I was making reference to the idea that there

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.190
are two dimensions Tadabbur (تدبر) before we,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.370
you know, went into further case studies of the Qur'an.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:26.060
The thing about Tadabbur is it's not an extra
superfluous kind of exercise. It has two functions.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.470
And both of those functions are mentioned by Allah by way of criticism.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.260
Meaning the consequence of not doing Tadabbur.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.860
The phrase occurring in the Qur'an is:

00:00:35.892 --> 00:00:37.260
أَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.560
Don't they then contemplate the Qur'an?

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.840
Don't they then reflect on the Qur'an?

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.550
Don't they seek the meaning behind the wording of the Qur'an? Okay?

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.160
But that's the opening statement 
أَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.170
The closing of that statement is two variations.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.710
So it occurs twice that statement in the Qur'an.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.040
And both times it says two different things.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.260
Not that's really interesting.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.959
One time Surat Mohammed Allah says:
أَمْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقْفَالُهَآ

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:09.350
Or is it the case that the hearts have their own locks placed on them?

00:01:10.987 --> 00:01:13.760
Or is it the case that the hearts have their own locks placed on them?

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.923
The Ayah, which we'll get into a little bit.
Before I do, just to give you the basics.

00:01:20.948 --> 00:01:27.460
Allah is saying not reflecting on the Qur'an is an indication of locks on hearts.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.460
Meaning not contemplating on the Qur'an is a spiritual problem.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.660
And contemplating on the Qur'an vice versa, what will it do?

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.050
It'll unlock hearts.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.860
It'll open hearts up.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:49.430
So the act of Tadabbur is directly related to the the the health of one's heart.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.160
It's a spiritual exercise. Okay?

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.283
If you look at the other case in the Qur'an:

00:01:55.308 --> 00:02:01.260
 أَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ ۚ وَلَوْ كَانَ مِنْ عِندِ غَيْرِ ٱللَّهِ لَوَجَدُواْ فِيهِ ٱخْتِلَٰفًا كَثِيرًا

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.450
Don't they then contemplate on the Qur'an?

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.340
Had it been from someone other than Allah,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.960
they would have found a lot of contradiction in it.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.320
Now Allah is saying: If you don't ponder the Qur'an,

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:17.560
it will appear as though the Qur'an has a lot of contradictions.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.710
And if you reflect on the Qur'an,

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.260
then you'll realize that it does not have

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:29.960
any contradictions. And actually you'll also realize that it can only be from Allah.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.350
Meaning your conviction that it is from Allah

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.360
will be strengthened and reinforced by way of what?

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.660
Contemplation.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.830
What does that mean then? That means that our Iman our faith is two things.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.160
It's in our hearts, and it's in our minds.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.340
Tadabbur in one Ayah fortifies the heart.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.410
Unlocks the heart and Tadabbur in the other Ayah gets rid of all the contradictions.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:56.170
Where do-- where does someone think about contradictions? Things not reconciling?

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.960
Is that a heart problem or a mind problem?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:58.560
Mhm.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.920
That's a mind problem.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.350
So Tadabbur on the Qur'an fortifies your faith intellectually.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.360
Gets rid of the contradictions.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.840
And Tadabbur on the Qur'an unlocks your heart.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:14.160
It's got a spiritual impact and it's got a uh, an intellectual impact.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:17.990
This is actually the two dimensions of our relationship with the Qur'an.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.000
This is it's, you know,

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.960
on the on the Manafi' (منافع) side. The benefit of the Qur'an is to your heart and to your mind.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.450
This is Allays says, for example,

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.548
about the people of the soundest mind. He says:

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.950
ٱلَّذِينَ يَذْكُرُونَ ٱللَّهَ قِيَٰمًا وَقُعُودًا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِهِمْ

00:03:31.974 --> 00:03:36.460
وَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِى خَلْقِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.469
[incorrect]

00:03:38.493 --> 00:03:40.493
رَبَّنَا مَا خَلَقْتَ هَٰذَا بَٰطِلًا

00:03:40.775 --> 00:03:43.280
Why? They remember Allah all the time; standing, sitting on their sides.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.660
Remembrance is in the heart.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.460
And they think about the creation of the skies in the earth. That's in the mind.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.750
Heart and mind.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.080
Reflection is about heart and mind.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.230
One Ayah is about reflection having to do with the heart,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.660
the other reflection having to do with the mind.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.460
I'm going to highlight the one with the heart just for a little bit.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.188
أَفَلَا يَتَدَبَّرُونَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ أَمْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقْفَالُهَآ

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:11.150
This Ayah, uh, interestingly it doesn't say: Don't they ponder on the Qur'an then?

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.180
Or do the hearts have locks on them? It doesn't say that.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.510
It says: Do the hearts have their own locks on them?

00:04:17.535 --> 00:04:19.415
(أَقْفَالُهَآ)

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.915
(أَمْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقْفَالٌ)

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.260
Or did the hearts have locks? No.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.160
Do they have their own locks?

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.530
There are some tendencies inside our hearts

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.960
that can get aggravated, that can get excited. And they can

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.060
lock us up like. There's no lock coming from the outside.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.460
The tendency to destroy ourselves exist from within.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.200
There are things that we put inside of us.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.910
There are appetites, desires, uh,

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.660
emotions that Allah put inside of us that can become self consuming.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.230
Anger is a healthy emotion,

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.560
but it can take over you.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.060
It could lock you up.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.660
Fear is a healthy emotion, but it could take over you, and it could lock you up.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.860
Sadness is a healthy emotion. You need it sometimes.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.360
But it can take over you. It can destroy you.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.850
At some level greed is important.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.270
At some level, you know,

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.190
aspiring to get more as part of getting up and earning a living.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.850
It's important but over-- too much greed and what's gonna happen?

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:16.760
It's gonna destroy you.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:22.260
The desire human-- men have for women or women have for men at some level is healthy.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.060
But if you let it take over you, it's gonna destroy you.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:30.050
The things that we put inside of our hearts, they can overwhelm and lock us up.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.880
One of the benefits of this Ayah is contemplating

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.560
on the Qur'an will actually keep our emotions in check.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.560
And not let those tendencies take over.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.500
Okay, that's one of one of the- like it'll create emotional balance.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.080
This is, in a sense, the Qur'an

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.280
also teaching that Qur'an is not just spiritual healing,

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.860
but it's also emotional healing.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.760
That our emotions are also put in check

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:55.100
and kept balanced because of our contemplation,

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.860
our engagement with Allah's Word.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.370
The other thing that I want to highlight here is

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:03.060
when you say their hearts, you know, let me use a figure of speech.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.260
Their heart is just made up.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.850
Their heart is a cement.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.690
When somebody has their mind made up,

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:12.250
they don't want to change their opinion about something.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:13.860
They're rigid.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.060
That's also an expression of a heart being locked.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.750
No matter what I do, they are not going to budge from their position.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.950
When you come to the Qur'an with presuppositions: I already know what it means.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:29.140
I'm only looking for the Daleel (دليل)
evidence

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.960
to further substantiate what I already know.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.050
Then you're not doing to the Tadabbur.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.950
Because you came to it with Aqfal (أَقْفَالُ).

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.940
You're not looking for what's behind the words because

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.160
you're assuming you already have what's behind the words.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:44.560
You understand.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:46.950
You have to let your preset positions go.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.270
You have to not look at the Qur'an-and unfortunately

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.630
even devout Muslims can become such that they're looking for Ayay to quote as someone.

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.960
Because they've already made up their mind what they want out of the Qur'an.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.860
I want this Ayah to slap my mother-in-law with.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.060
Can you find me something?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.980
I want something to say about these people who said this, this and this.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.230
I want to say something to my brother who did this that

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.300
the other day. Where is the Ayah? I've already made up my mind

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.460
what I'm going to get out of the Qur'an. My locks already there.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:22.320
Therefore, I'm not looking for the Qur'an to-- for me to serve Allah's Word. And to me--

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.800
for me to be at the service of Allah's Word.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:29.350
But rather I want my locked up heart to, you know, for it to be served.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.360
Buy some references.

00:07:32.143 --> 00:07:33.750
Don't they ponder the Qur'an?

00:07:34.089 --> 00:07:36.195
 أَمْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبٍ أَقْفَالُهَآ

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.860
So may Allah protect us from that spiritual crisis. Okay.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:44.350
I want to take you to our next case study. And that is Surat al-Qiyamah.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.970
And it is an interesting,

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:51.140
really interesting transition in Ayat that is very clearly unrelated.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.880
Like at the face value, it couldn't be more unrelated.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:56.450
So I'm going to read the translation from the beginning once again.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.210
So you know what the subject matter is about and then get to the Ayat

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:03.250
that clearly have nothing to do with the rest of the subject at face value.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.450
لا أُقْسِمُ بِيَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ
No! I swear by the Day of Standing, Resurrection.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.160
وَلا
And no!

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:13.620
أُقْسِمُ بِالنَّفْسِ اللَّوَّامَةِ
 I take an oath.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:19.260
I swear by the guilty self. The self that blames one's own over and over.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.600
أَيَحْسَبُ الإِنسَانُ أَلَّن نَجْمَعَ عِظَامَهُ

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.660
Has the human being assumed that We're not going to gather his bones together?

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:30.100
بَلَى 
Of course 
قَادِرِينَ عَلَى أَن نُّسَوِّيَ بَنَانَهُ

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:34.760
We are capable of even putting his bones, his fingertips back together.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:37.611
بَلْ يُرِيدُ الإِنسَانُ لِيَفْجُرَ أَمَامَهُ

00:08:37.636 --> 00:08:41.894
Instead the human being just wants to explode into whatever comes in front of him.

00:08:41.919 --> 00:08:43.210
Basically saying the human being is

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.460
just impulsive. Human beings don't care about the Day of Judgment.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:49.340
They don't care about resurrection because they're too busy

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.520
jumping into what is right in front of them.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.640
What's the next party? What's the next app? What's the next game?

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:55.560
What's the next movie?

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:58.729
They're just immediately into the next, the next, the next the next (يَفْجُرَ أَمَامَهُ).

00:08:58.754 --> 00:09:03.550
يَسْأَلُ أَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الْقِيَامَةِ
And he has the audacity to ask: when

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.640
come on, when is the day of resurrection anyway?

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.660
Why are you talking to me about that right now? I have something I want to do right now.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.576
That's when it is we'll deal with it.

00:09:11.601 --> 00:09:15.463
فَإِذَا بَرِقَ الْبَصَرُ
وَخَسَفَ الْقَمَرُ
وَجُمِعَ الشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:21.060
And then all of a sudden, when eyes are flinching because of the flashes

00:09:21.541 --> 00:09:26.960
وَخَسَفَ الْقَمَرُ
They're blinded by the flashes. And the the moon starts sinking.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.321
وَجُمِعَ الشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ
And the sun and the moon

00:09:29.346 --> 00:09:31.080
have merged with each other.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.545
يَقُولُ الإِنسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍ أَيْنَ الْمَفَرُّ

00:09:33.664 --> 00:09:36.530
Then the human being, the same
human being who's saying: When is it coming?

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:37.960
When is it coming? Come on!

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.260
Is going to say: Where can I run off to?

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.605
كَلاَّ 
No, no, no.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.824
لا وَزَرَ
There is no place to find refuge.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:49.439
There's no barrier. There's no barricade between you and that Day.

00:09:49.464 --> 00:09:53.500
إِلَى رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ الْمُسْتَقَرُّ
To your Master alone on that Day

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:55.450
is going to be the place where you have to stay.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.170
To come and stand.

00:09:57.289 --> 00:10:01.680
يُنَبَّأُ الإِنسَانُ يَوْمَئِذٍ  
The human being will be informed thoroughly on that day

00:10:01.705 --> 00:10:06.150
بِمَا قَدَّمَ وَأَخَّرَ
whatever priorities he made, whatever procrastination he did.

00:10:06.638 --> 00:10:09.200
Whatever took the front seat. Whatever took the backseat.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:13.269
He's going to be told thoroughly.
بَلِ الإِنسَانُ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ بَصِيرَةٌ

00:10:13.294 --> 00:10:16.437
Instead the human being even
now is in full view of his own self.

00:10:16.461 --> 00:10:17.830
وَلَوْ أَلْقَى مَعَاذِيرَهُ

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:19.960
Even though he keeps throwing out excuses.

00:10:21.002 --> 00:10:24.360
Now so far, it's about people who are skeptical about Judgment Day.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:27.460
And how shocked they are going to be when it does come

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:31.460
And how not not concerned about it they are right now.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:35.870
Now listen [لا تُحَرِّكْ] this is the part that's apparently not related.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:40.850
لا تُحَرِّكْ بِهِ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهِ
Do not rush your tongue

00:10:41.736 --> 00:10:46.160
by the Qur'an using it, meaning the Qur'an, so you can acquire it quickly.

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:49.860
Don't move your tongue to acquire the Qur'an quickly.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.360
Who's is it talking to?

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:52.880
The Prophet ﷺ.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:57.440
The Prophet is concerned he's gonna lose
Qur'an, so he's trying to rush to memorize it.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:00.393
And Allah is saying: Don't move
your tongue like that to get it quickly.

00:11:00.417 --> 00:11:02.070
إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا جَمْعَهُ وَقُرْآنَهُ

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.660
It is only Our responsibility

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:04.950
to have it gathered

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.250
and have it recited. You remember this Ayah from yesterday.

00:11:07.996 --> 00:11:10.535
فَإِذَا قَرَأْنَاهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْآنَهُ

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:11.750
And when We have it recited,

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.060
then just follow it.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.680
Then follow that recitation.
ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا بَيَانَهُ

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:21.040
And certainly it is only Our responsibility to clarify it.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:24.160
This is a conversation between Allah and the Prophet, telling the Prophet ﷺ

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.260
Don't you worry. I'll take care of the Qur'an.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.303
Now listen
كَلاَّ بَلْ تُحِبُّونَ الْعَاجِلَةَ

00:11:29.327 --> 00:11:32.180
No, no, no.
But you people love to rush. You love

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:34.910
you love things that come immediately. Going back to

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.180
the people of this world who are unconcerned

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:39.460
with the next world, where the Surah began.

00:11:40.013 --> 00:11:41.220
وَتَذَرُونَ الآخِرَةَ

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:43.494
And you leave the afterlife behind.

00:11:43.518 --> 00:11:45.656
وُجُوهٌ يَوْمَئِذٍ نَّاضِرَةٌ

00:11:45.681 --> 00:11:47.550
Some people will be lit on that Day.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.238
إِلَى رَبِّهَا نَاظِرَةٌ
Staring at their Master.

00:11:50.263 --> 00:11:52.010
وَوُجُوهٌ يَوْمَئِذٍ بَاسِرَةٌ

00:11:52.071 --> 00:11:54.285
تَظُنُّ أَن يُفْعَلَ بِهَا فَاقِرَةٌ

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.260
Some people--some faces will be overwhelmed with grief.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:01.640
They're gonna keep assuming that some calamity is about to hit them. Strike them.

00:12:01.665 --> 00:12:03.340
كَلاَّ إِذَا بَلَغَتْ التَّرَاقِيَ

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:09.160
وَقِيلَ مَنْ رَاقٍ
No, no, no. When when it reaches all the way to the tip of the throat

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:13.531
and it's gonna cry out. Is there any (رَاقٍ)? Is there any reciter?

00:12:13.556 --> 00:12:16.958
Doctor? Anyone can help?
There's an emergency. This is a (رَاقٍ).

00:12:16.982 --> 00:12:18.250
You know Ruqya (رقية)?

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.760
Right. Can someone recite something to help me out here?

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.740
وَظَنَّ أَنَّهُ الْفِرَاقُ

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.410
And it'll dawn on him that it's the time to part ways.

00:12:26.465 --> 00:12:28.128
وَالْتَفَّتِ السَّاقُ بِالسَّاقِ

00:12:28.152 --> 00:12:31.280
And his heels are going to
start rubbing against each other.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:33.390
This is a person dying in bed.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:36.750
Their body's arching in pain and their legs are you know,

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.356
they're rubbing against
each other as they're dying.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.960
وَالْتَفَّتِ السَّاقُ بِالسَّاقِ

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.080
إِلَى رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ الْمَسَاقُ

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.235
You're about to be herded only towards your Master now.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:47.730
فَلا صَدَّقَ وَلا صَلَّى

00:12:47.905 --> 00:12:49.391
وَلَكِن كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلَّى

00:12:49.415 --> 00:12:52.400
He was-- he didn't confirm
the truth, nor did he pray.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.524
Instead, he called it a
lie. And he turned his back.

00:12:54.603 --> 00:12:57.420
And the Surah goes on again Akhira, Akhira, Akhira.

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:59.825
What's the only subject that didn't have to do with the Akhira?

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:00.860
The afterlife?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:04.560
The rushing of the Prophet ﷺ to acquire more Qur'an.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.470
This is when understanding the entire Surah as a

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.200
whole helps us understand each component in each part.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:10.850
Okay?

00:13:12.367 --> 00:13:14.510
They are clearly very defiant about the message

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.670
of the Akhira. Is, according to the Prophet ﷺ

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.660
and what he's been taught, is the Day of Judgment near or far?

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:21.184
It's near.

00:13:21.209 --> 00:13:24.250
إِنَّهُمْ يَرَوْنَهُ بَعِيدًا وَنَرَاهُ قَرِيبًا
It's near.

00:13:24.945 --> 00:13:26.563
The Prophet ﷺ is reciting Qur'an to them.

00:13:26.587 --> 00:13:28.530
He is giving them these Ayat, these evidences.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.260
Are they taking those evidences seriously?

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:31.300
No.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.390
The Prophet ﷺ is concerned

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:37.360
that may be the Ayat that I gave them now did not convince them.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.250
Maybe some other Ayat will, and maybe some other

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.750
Ayat will, and maybe some other Ayat will.

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:44.260
And the Prophet ﷺ is in a rush to convince

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.690
them in some way that they can change course.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.730
Maybe it's not becoming clear to them.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.260
Maybe some other Ayat will make it clearer to them.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:54.940
Because one way didn't work.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:58.340
I tried to explain it to them by these Ayat, and they just dismissed it.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:01.710
May be the next Surah will help. Maybe the next Ayat will help.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:04.000
So he's quickly acquiring them and trying to rush

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.860
to get to more and to more and to more.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:09.730
So that he can get them to change course. Because he knows how close it is.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.360
How close their destruction is.

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:16.060
And here they are, unconcerned.
أَيَّانَ يَوْمُ القيامة

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:21.190
The Prophet's rushing is highlighted here to to to to

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:26.360
demonstrate how desperate he feels at how unconcerned they are.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:31.140
But now I want you to appreciate. As as soon as Allah criticized the Prophet's rushing.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.270
Don't you rush? That's not onto you. That's not up to you.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:37.050
And by the way, you rushing is not why it's not clear to them.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:44.150
Why? [ثُمَّ إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا بَيَانَهُ] It is only Our responsibility to make it clear.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:49.550
That's not up to you. We've already made--the words are clear in and of themselves.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:52.500
You reciting more of it is not going to make it more clear.

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:54.480
It's a really profound wisdom inside of these

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:58.100
Ayat that when you talk to somebody and they're

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.150
not convinced about what advice you're trying to give them.

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:03.418
Sometimes you think: What
other Hadith can I quote?

00:15:03.442 --> 00:15:05.260
What other Ayah can I give them?

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.000
What other Daleel (دليل) can I throw at them?

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.848
Maybe that'll work,. And then you
send an email to a Sheikh or whatever:

00:15:09.872 --> 00:15:12.210
Is there--you know
I was having a discussion with my mom.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:16.050
She doesn't agree with me. What can I tell her more about fearing Allah?

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.050
Uh, that's not how that works.

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.560
That's not how that works.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.459
You know, you can't just quote more things, give more Ayat.

00:15:23.484 --> 00:15:25.350
That's not that's not where the problem lies.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:26.460
You know?

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.860
And so

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.650
after having said Allah says something remarkable.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.191
This is the irony of this Surah.

00:15:32.216 --> 00:15:34.760
كَلاَّ بَلْ تُحِبُّونَ الْعَاجِلَةَ
Same word.

00:15:35.679 --> 00:15:39.450
He was told 
لا تُحَرِّكْ بِهِ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهِ

00:15:40.091 --> 00:15:43.040
Allah swicthes the subject. Turns to the people he's so worried about.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.940
And says you people love to rush.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:48.590
Mufassirun look at this Ayah and say "love to rush means" love

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.500
what comes quickly. And what comes quickly is this life.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:54.260
And what's going to come after a while is the next life.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:57.460
So this is Allah's way of saying you people love this life.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.560
But Allah could have just as easily said ad-Dunya.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.876
كلا بل تحبون (الدنيا)
He said:

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.380
كَلاَّ بَلْ تُحِبُّونَ الْعَاجِلَةَ

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:10.960
The thing that comes quickly. What benefit does that carry and how is it connected?

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:11.740
You see,

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:15.310
the Qur'an is saying that when you are defiant of the Prophet ﷺ.

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.360
And when you ask questions like when is Judgment Day coming.

00:16:19.907 --> 00:16:22.660
Then the Qur'an will describe it as: 
يَسْتَعْجِلُونَكَ بِٱلْعَذَابِ

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:24.740
By being this defiant

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.660
it's like they want to rush the punishment towards themselves.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:30.740
Have you ever seen, like,

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:32.360
let me--give you by analogy.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.060
Kids misbehaving?

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:37.660
And then the parent says: Oh, you really want it now, don't you?

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.860
You know you want to get it right now, don't you?

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:41.760
What is the parents saying?

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.150
Oh, you're about to get

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.860
you know, a good talk?

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:51.850
Not if you're in Pakistan.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:52.660
Okay.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.970
You're about to get a different kind of education.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:59.560
Meaning? Oh, yeah. Keep it up. Oh, you love rushing, don't you?

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.360
You'd like to, you'd like to bring it quickly, wouldn't you?

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.210
It's as though Allah is

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:10.060
contrasting the Prophet's urgency to pull them away with

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:13.359
their idiotic urgency to go towards the same fire

00:17:13.359 --> 00:17:14.460
the Prophet's pulling them out of.

00:17:15.878 --> 00:17:17.770
And then Allah says Himself:

00:17:18.339 --> 00:17:19.980
This rush that you have

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:23.130
that you're you know,

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:26.500
you-- the rush that you have that you're not going to be those lit faces.

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.760
You're going to be the darkened faces. You don't have to wait until that happens.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.550
What about your own death? That's not that far away.

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:37.710
And the moment the death comes when the soul is about to reach--leave your bodies

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:39.310
then you're not going to be in a rush.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.528
Then you're gonna be begging for someone who can slow this down.

00:17:41.553 --> 00:17:43.060
وَقِيلَ مَنْ رَاقٍ

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.321
Where's where's your 'Ujla (عجلة) now?

00:17:45.346 --> 00:17:47.160
Where's the 'Ajila (عاجلة) now? It's gone.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:52.660
So this is actually highlighting in the middle of a Surah that, you know,

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:56.470
that that describes the defiance of those who don't believe in the Akhira,

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:58.160
the concern of the Prophet ﷺ.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:03.230
And this is-it's not in a literary sense, in a psychological sense.

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:05.650
Understand that the Qur'an has multiple audiences.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:08.110
Allah is giving this message to the Quraysh.

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:10.976
But who's giving that message, is Rasulallah ﷺ.

00:18:11.001 --> 00:18:14.190
And he has to be in the middle. Just come down. I got this.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.760
I'm gonna get this message to them, but you need to hold your come.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:20.650
Don't you rush. That's not your responsibility. That's My responsibility.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.860
You just deliver the reminder as I give it to you.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.000
And then go back to the reminder.

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:28.770
This beautiful transition actually even reminds us in the middle of this

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:32.060
discourse that this discourse is not invented by the Prophet ﷺ.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:37.050
Right? That this conversation is authentic, that it is coming from the Allah. Okay?

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.520
So that was some of the benefit of- by the way some have also argued like

00:18:41.545 --> 00:18:44.210
Imam Razi about this transition. This particular one.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:48.270
Uh, he argued that Allah does not like rushing of any kind.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.200
Not people who rush into worldly things and

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:53.770
and not people who rush into even religious things.

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:56.270
Even the Prophet is told to slow down with the Qur'an.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.170
So one shouldn't rush with the Qur'an.

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:03.030
So that's kind of a side benefit that he mentions of the placement of these Ayat.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:04.272
Okay, I'm gonna move on Inshallah

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:08.560
to the next case study. Probably one last one before we take the break for the prayer.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.450
Let me see how many I have left.

00:19:11.340 --> 00:19:12.770
Oh, man, that one's juicy.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.060
The last one.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:20.450
Uh, yeah. Okay, there's two more left in this.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:22.550
But we'll do one more Inshallah right now.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:26.010
All right, so this is Surat al-'Ankabut.

00:19:26.035 --> 00:19:27.850
Surah number 29. The beginning.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:30.560
Let me give you some context.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.460
So you appreciate what's going on in Surah number 29.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:38.860
Uh, torture has now become part of the way that Quraysh deal with the Muslims.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.260
Okay? They're trying to-they're now starting to become physically

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.270
hurtful, offensive.

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:45.730
Towards the Muslims.

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:47.850
People are being beat up. People are being burned.

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:51.810
People are being tortured, stepped on, tied up, half buried into the ground,

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:52.530
etcetera, etcetera.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.330
There's there's all kinds of things that are being

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:57.430
done to people because they have now become Muslim.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.050
And in response to that,

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:00.850
Uh, this Surah came.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:05.430
So keep that in the back of your mind as you look at

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:09.550
Allah's way of helping the Muslims through this crisis situation in late Makkah.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:11.209
الم

00:20:11.234 --> 00:20:14.560
أَحَسِبَ النَّاسُ أَن يُتْرَكُوا أَن يَقُولُوا آمَنَّا وَهُمْ لا يُفْتَنُونَ

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:16.870
Alif Lam Mim. Have people assume that they're going

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:19.170
to be left alone just because they say they believed?

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:22.360
And they're not going to be put through intense testing?

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.120
وَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا الَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:27.479
We thoroughly tested
those who came before them

00:20:27.503 --> 00:20:29.531
فَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ صَدَقُوا

00:20:29.556 --> 00:20:32.476
Then certainly Allah exposed those who were truthful

00:20:32.516 --> 00:20:34.310
[gibberish]

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:37.350
وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ الْكَاذِبِينَ
Allah certainly will expose the liars.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.415
أَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ السَّيِّئَاتِ أَن يَسْبِقُونَا

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:44.860
Have those who committed crimes assumed that they  got ahead of us?

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:46.171
They got away from us?

00:20:46.195 --> 00:20:46.935
سَاء مَا يَحْكُمُونَ

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:48.550
What a horrible decision they've made.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.680
So on the one hand Allah says to the believers: Look,

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.270
did you think you're not going to be tested?

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:56.770
And at the same time He says: Do you think they're getting away with what they do?

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.360
They're not getting away.

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:03.490
مَن كَانَ يَرْجُو لِقَاء اللَّهِ فَإِنَّ أَجَلَ اللَّهِ لَآتٍ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.090
Whoever was hopeful of meeting with Allah

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.530
then you should know that the meeting of Allah

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:10.450
is on its way. He is All Hearing, All Knowing.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.260
If you were hopeful for relief, escape

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:16.050
other refuge, then you were hoping for the wrong thing.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:19.550
You came into this Deen to hope for the meeting with Allah.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.750
So I'm making it clear for you.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:24.295
وَمَن جَاهَدَ فَإِنَّمَا يُجَاهِدُ لِنَفْسِهِ

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.488
And whoever is struggling is only doing so
for his own benefit.

00:21:27.512 --> 00:21:29.041
إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَغَنِيٌّ عَنِ الْعَالَمِينَ

00:21:29.066 --> 00:21:30.860
Allah doesn't need your sacrifices.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:32.860
He's free of need of all nations and all peoples.

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:36.360
The Sahaba, as incredible as their sacrifices are,

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:38.550
Allah doesn't say:

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.000
Don't you let the thought come in your

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.060
mind that you're somehow contributing to Islam.

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:44.060
I don't need you.

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:46.270
You can go back if you want.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:48.470
All the struggle you're doing is your own self.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.550
You're not benefiting me. You're benefiting yourself.

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.170
What a reality check like.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.170
We're not doing this for Allah.

00:21:57.640 --> 00:22:00.900
What does that even mean? We're doing it for ourselves.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.460
And don't you forget it.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.680
You're not doing anybody a favor.

00:22:04.704 --> 00:22:06.206
وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ

00:22:06.231 --> 00:22:10.630
And those who-- then then after the harsh reality check. Tough love.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.770
Then there's soft love.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:16.200
He says: And those who do--Those who believe and act righteously, do good deeds.

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:18.060
لَنُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّئَاتِهِمْ

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:21.250
We will absolutely bury away from them all of their sins.

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:23.665
وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّهُمْ أَحْسَنَ الَّذِي كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:26.340
And We will compensate them with the best of what they used to do.

00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:28.360
وَوَصَّيْنَا الإِنسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حُسْنًا

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:30.600
Then there's physical torture, there's psychological torture.

00:22:30.610 --> 00:22:33.680
Some of the companions were being not physically beat, but their mother was saying:

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:36.320
If you don't, if you don't leave Islam, I'll stop eating.

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:39.260
If you don't leave Islam, I'll kill myself etcetera, etcetera.

00:22:39.340 --> 00:22:41.090
What kind of son are you? What son

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:42.850
or what daughter can hear that from their parents?

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:44.580
So Allah says: We counseled

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:47.755
the human being to be good,
especially to both his parents.

00:22:47.779 --> 00:22:51.190
وَإِن جَاهَدَاكَ لِتُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:52.620
And if they're struggling against you,

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:55.713
they're they're they're resisting against
you to make you commit Shirk.

00:22:55.737 --> 00:22:59.952
Over what you know there's no
knowledge for. You have no knowledge of it.

00:22:59.977 --> 00:23:02.270
فَلا تُطِعْهُمَا
Then don't obey them.

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:03.760
Don't obey either of them.

00:23:03.784 --> 00:23:04.720
إِلَيَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.360
You're you're going to all be returned to me; parents and yourself.

00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:10.721
فَأُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ

00:23:10.746 --> 00:23:13.450
And I will inform you in detail what you used to do.

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:14.910
وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:17.960
By the way, if the parents are not obeyed, what's going to happen to those people?

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:19.950
They're gonna get disowned.

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:22.458
And so, as soon as they get disowned Allah says:

00:23:22.482 --> 00:23:25.734
وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ لَنُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ فِي الصَّالِحِينَ

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:27.930
Those who believe and do good deeds.

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:30.840
We will We will give them the new company. We will make--

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:34.350
enter them the company of the righteous. You lost one family. I'll give you a new one.

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:35.950
You see how it's connected.

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:39.140
وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ آمَنَّا بِاللَّ

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:43.140
And among people there are those who started off saying they believe in Allah

00:23:43.270 --> 00:23:47.890
فَإِذَا أُوذِيَ فِي اللَّ
and the moment that torture began in their path to Allah

00:23:48.020 --> 00:23:51.960
جَعَلَ فِتْنَةَ النَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ اللَّهِ
the fact that people were giving them a hard time,

00:23:51.970 --> 00:23:55.060
they assume that to mean that Allah is punishing them.

00:23:55.440 --> 00:23:57.600
You know, when I wasn't following Islam, things were good.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:24:00.560
As soon as I started following Islam, life became miserable.

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:03.640
It's like Allah doesn't want me to do this.

00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:06.060
It's like Allah is punishing me for becoming more Islamic.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:10.600
Allah is--this is literally mirroring some people's life situations

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:11.850
you know that like.

00:24:11.874 --> 00:24:13.296
جَعَلَ فِتْنَةَ النَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ اللَّهِ

00:24:13.320 --> 00:24:15.960
when people give them a hard time, they say: This is Allah punishing me.

00:24:17.240 --> 00:24:19.880
And when I stopped praying, when I went back to drinking and whatever else

00:24:19.880 --> 00:24:20.630
things got better.

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.800
Problems disappeared. It's every time I start, you know, coming closer to God then

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:28.350
all hell breaks loose. Something's wrong with it.

00:24:28.840 --> 00:24:30.460
وَلَئِن جَاءَ نَصْرٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ

00:24:31.140 --> 00:24:34.990
And by the way, the same people when aid comes from your Rabb, when relief does come

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:35.430
they said:

00:24:35.454 --> 00:24:36.956
لَيَقُولُنَّ إِنَّا كُنَّا مَعَكُمْ

00:24:36.981 --> 00:24:39.770
No, no, no. We were always with you. I've
always had really strong faith, you know?

00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:42.670
I am a really spiritual person.

00:24:43.140 --> 00:24:45.360
Except when times are hard then I'm not, but.

00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:47.160
Other than that I'm really spiritual.

00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:50.264
أَوَلَيْسَ اللَّهُ بِأَعْلَمَ بِمَا فِي صُدُورِ الْعَالَمِينَ

00:24:50.289 --> 00:24:52.457
Does Allah not
know-doesn't He know

00:24:52.481 --> 00:24:55.660
better? What truly lies in
the chests of all peoples?

00:24:55.670 --> 00:24:58.625
وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ

00:24:58.650 --> 00:25:01.670
Allah will expose those who truly believe and Allah will expose hypocrites.

00:25:02.589 --> 00:25:04.810
That's a form of hypocrisy. 
وَقَالَ الَّذِينَ

00:25:04.820 --> 00:25:08.100
Then the next form of pressure and torture. There was physical torture.

00:25:08.110 --> 00:25:10.542
There's family torture. Now
there's social peer pressure.

00:25:10.566 --> 00:25:13.770
وَقَالَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّبِعُوا سَبِيلَنَا

00:25:14.640 --> 00:25:16.060
Disbelievers said to believers:

00:25:16.060 --> 00:25:18.360
Why don't you just follow the way we used to follow; our way?

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:20.285
وَلْنَحْمِلْ خَطَايَاكُمْ

00:25:20.310 --> 00:25:21.860
We will carry your sins.

00:25:22.740 --> 00:25:26.160
Why are you why are you hurting yourself-- Elders of Quraysh would come.

00:25:26.740 --> 00:25:28.270
And say to the Sahaba: Listen,

00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:29.710
I'm an elder.

00:25:30.140 --> 00:25:32.540
I've seen a lot of things. This is not the right religion.

00:25:32.550 --> 00:25:34.170
If you're so worried that it's the right religion

00:25:34.170 --> 00:25:36.370
and you're sinning by coming back to your senses.

00:25:36.410 --> 00:25:39.050
Then let me tell you, I guarantee if God does question

00:25:39.050 --> 00:25:41.560
I'll say he did it because of me. I'll carry your sins.

00:25:41.940 --> 00:25:43.950
Okay? Is that okay now? Now come on back.

00:25:44.460 --> 00:25:45.360
Now stop being silly.

00:25:46.701 --> 00:25:47.640
So now He says:

00:25:47.664 --> 00:25:51.060
وَلْنَحْمِلْ خَطَايَاكُمْ وَمَا هُم بِحَامِلِينَ مِنْ خَطَايَاهُم مِّن شَيْءٍ

00:25:51.070 --> 00:25:53.785
And they're not going to be carrying any of
their mistakes in any way, shape or form.

00:25:53.810 --> 00:25:54.925
إِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ

00:25:54.958 --> 00:25:56.260
They're absolutely liars.

00:25:56.640 --> 00:25:59.650
This is peer pressure from elders who've been respected one's whole life.

00:25:59.650 --> 00:26:02.780
And now you became Muslim, and all of a sudden you're like: you know how old I am,

00:26:02.780 --> 00:26:03.060
right?

00:26:03.070 --> 00:26:04.050
You know how wise I am?

00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:07.560
You know, I've given you advice in your life, and you're not gonna listen to this?

00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:11.000
You don't get it right now. You're under a lot of pressure.

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:13.430
I understand that you were depressed and that's why you fell into this cult

00:26:13.430 --> 00:26:16.960
called Islam. But come to your senses. If even if it is bad

00:26:16.960 --> 00:26:17.870
I'll carry your sins.

00:26:17.880 --> 00:26:19.251
And Allah says they're lying.

00:26:19.276 --> 00:26:20.806
وَلَيَحْمِلُنَّ أَثْقَالَهُمْ

00:26:20.830 --> 00:26:22.809
They will carry their own heavy
loads.

00:26:22.833 --> 00:26:24.220
وَأَثْقَالا مَّعَ أَثْقَالِهِمْ

00:26:24.220 --> 00:26:26.670
and they'll carry loads along with their own loads.

00:26:27.540 --> 00:26:30.005
وَلَيُسْأَلُنَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ عَمَّا كَانُوا يَفْتَرُونَ

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:32.190
And they're going to be interrogated about what they used

00:26:32.190 --> 00:26:34.260
to make up. All of this was clearly connected.

00:26:35.510 --> 00:26:38.910
Now all of a sudden, without warning, a jump to  stories of prophets.

00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:42.239
وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا إِلَى قَوْمِهِ

00:26:42.264 --> 00:26:45.230
Nuh stayed with his people--We sent him to his people.

00:26:45.240 --> 00:26:47.960
فَلَبِثَ فِيهِمْ أَلْفَ سَنَةٍ إِلاَّ خَمْسِينَ عَامًا

00:26:48.640 --> 00:26:49.660
He stayed with them

00:26:50.430 --> 00:26:52.521
1000 years saved just 50.

00:26:52.546 --> 00:26:54.770
فَأَخَذَهُمُ الطُّوفَانُ وَهُمْ ظَالِمُونَ

00:26:54.794 --> 00:26:55.740
Then a punishment--

00:26:55.750 --> 00:26:58.590
the storm got to them and they were-- while they were doing wrong.

00:26:58.600 --> 00:27:01.915
فَأَنجَيْنَاهُ وَأَصْحَابَ السَّفِينَةِ وَجَعَلْنَاهَا آيَةً لِّلْعَالَمِينَ

00:27:01.940 --> 00:27:05.150
We rescued him and the people on the ship, on the Ark.

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:07.880
And We made them into a miracle for all nations and peoples.

00:27:07.890 --> 00:27:09.360
[وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ] now another prophet.

00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:13.550
[وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ] And Ibrahim 'alaihissalam 
إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ وَاتَّقُوهُ

00:27:13.550 --> 00:27:18.170
when he said, worship Allah and follow him-- and obey and be mindful of him.

00:27:18.640 --> 00:27:20.765
ذَلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ
إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ

00:27:20.789 --> 00:27:22.450
That's better for you if you knew.

00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:25.830
So first prophet mentioned in transition was what? Nuh.

00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:29.030
Then? Ibrahim 'alaihissalam. And I'm gonna skip a little bit.

00:27:29.040 --> 00:27:32.370
And I'll go to just Ibrahim 'alaihissalam gives them a long speech.

00:27:32.380 --> 00:27:33.770
And at the end of that speech

00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:38.360
فَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهِ
And what was the response of his people?

00:27:38.385 --> 00:27:41.360
إِلاَّ أَن قَالُوا اقْتُلُوهُ أَوْ حَرِّقُوهُ

00:27:41.840 --> 00:27:44.660
These people only responded by saying kill him or burn him alive.

00:27:45.540 --> 00:27:46.773
فَأَنجَاهُ اللَّهُ مِنَ النَّارِ

00:27:46.798 --> 00:27:48.503
Allah rescue him from the fire.

00:27:48.527 --> 00:27:50.565
إِنَّ فِي ذَلِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ

00:27:50.590 --> 00:27:55.170
And certainly there are miraculous signs for those who truly are seeking to believe.

00:27:55.195 --> 00:27:57.705
وَقَالَ إِنَّمَا اتَّخَذْتُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّهِ أَوْثَانًا مَّوَدَّةَ

00:27:57.730 --> 00:27:59.270
بَيْنِكُمْ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا

00:27:59.740 --> 00:28:04.890
And he even said: This--All these gods you've taken other than Allah

00:28:04.890 --> 00:28:07.960
this is just you keeping, keeping up with each other.

00:28:08.740 --> 00:28:12.240
You're like you're not really holding onto the religion. You're just more worried

00:28:12.240 --> 00:28:13.560
mom is gonna be really upset.

00:28:14.540 --> 00:28:16.962
So that's why 
مَّوَدَّةَ بَيْنِكُمْ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا

00:28:16.987 --> 00:28:19.752
Just out of love for the other
you hold on to the false religion.

00:28:19.776 --> 00:28:21.370
Not because you actually believe it.

00:28:21.380 --> 00:28:23.000
He called them out on it. Somebody

00:28:23.025 --> 00:28:25.713
ثُمَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ يَكْفُرُ بَعْضُكُم بِبَعْضٍ

00:28:25.738 --> 00:28:28.604
 And when Judgment Day comes, you'll be denying each other.

00:28:28.640 --> 00:28:30.780
The same people for which you held onto falsehood

00:28:30.790 --> 00:28:32.770
will be the same people you'll be absolutely rejecting

00:28:32.770 --> 00:28:33.584
on Judgment Day.

00:28:33.609 --> 00:28:35.960
وَيَلْعَنُ بَعْضُكُم بَعْضًا
And you'll be cursing each other then.

00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:38.357
وَمَأْوَاكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا
لَكُم مِّن نَّاصِرِينَ

00:28:38.381 --> 00:28:40.760
And then your place will be
fire. You won't have any helpers.

00:28:41.540 --> 00:28:43.270
فَآمَنَ لَهُ لُوطٌ

00:28:43.840 --> 00:28:46.170
Another prophet now. Which prophet?

00:28:46.540 --> 00:28:48.360
وَقَالَ إِنِّي مُهَاجِرٌ إِلَى رَبِّي

00:28:49.040 --> 00:28:50.990
He said: I'm making migration to my Master.

00:28:51.100 --> 00:28:52.570
إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ

00:28:52.940 --> 00:28:54.430
Certainly He is the Mighty, the Wise.

00:28:54.940 --> 00:28:57.170
So the thing to understand is the first

00:28:57.170 --> 00:28:59.270
passage had to do with torture intensifying and

00:28:59.270 --> 00:29:01.790
the trials that the Muslims are going through in Makkah. And all of a sudden

00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:03.460
Nuh, Ibrahim, Lut.

00:29:04.340 --> 00:29:05.210
Understand this:

00:29:05.740 --> 00:29:09.550
Nuh 'alaihissalam escaped the punishment of water.

00:29:11.340 --> 00:29:13.860
Ibrahim 'alaihissalam escaped the punishment of

00:29:14.340 --> 00:29:15.170
fire.

00:29:16.740 --> 00:29:19.770
Lut 'alaihissalam came out and said: I am making Hijrah.

00:29:20.740 --> 00:29:23.310
All three of them migrated away from

00:29:23.310 --> 00:29:25.310
disbelievers that were putting them through trial.

00:29:25.310 --> 00:29:25.860
Yes or no?

00:29:26.440 --> 00:29:26.940
Yeah.

00:29:27.510 --> 00:29:29.860
The Sahaba are going through intense trials.

00:29:30.340 --> 00:29:31.170
In Makkah.

00:29:32.140 --> 00:29:33.090
In Makkah.

00:29:33.200 --> 00:29:37.170
If Allah comes out publicly and says: Why don't you just all go to Medina?

00:29:38.140 --> 00:29:39.160
Can they?

00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:41.460
They have to go secretly.

00:29:42.540 --> 00:29:43.950
Don't they have to go secretly.

00:29:44.740 --> 00:29:48.060
So Allah 'azzawajal speaks in prophetic story code.

00:29:49.140 --> 00:29:50.380
And tells them: Let Me tell

00:29:50.380 --> 00:29:56.030
Nuh 'alaihissalam stayed among his people 1000 years except for-- 950 years.

00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:59.160
A long time. Sahaba will say: We've lived here our whole life. Where we gonna go?

00:29:59.940 --> 00:30:03.360
Allah says Nuh was in his people for 1000 years and We got him out.

00:30:04.840 --> 00:30:05.730
And We ruined them.

00:30:05.740 --> 00:30:06.440
It's as though,

00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:11.450
and by the way Allah describes those people that they will be carrying their burdens.

00:30:11.460 --> 00:30:12.630
Allah describes them:

00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:15.670
You think they got away. Meaning punishment is coming to this town.

00:30:16.540 --> 00:30:18.460
And it's time for believers to what?

00:30:19.040 --> 00:30:19.850
Leave.

00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:21.860
Just like Nuh left.

00:30:22.340 --> 00:30:23.080
And by the way,

00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:25.590
Ibrahim 'alaihissalam challenges people with the

00:30:25.590 --> 00:30:27.420
same things you're challenging your people with.

00:30:27.430 --> 00:30:31.030
And they were ready to burn him alive and to to kill him.

00:30:31.040 --> 00:30:33.860
And things look like they're getting to that point with you, too.

00:30:34.240 --> 00:30:36.740
And if I can get Ibrahim--Nuh 'alaihissalam

00:30:36.740 --> 00:30:41.030
out of water that covered the earth and I can get Ibrahim

00:30:41.030 --> 00:30:43.060
'alaihissalam out of fire that should burn.

00:30:43.440 --> 00:30:44.460
I'm gonna get you out.

00:30:45.140 --> 00:30:48.920
And if it's not clear what I'm trying to get across to you just listen.

00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:52.060
Lut 'alaihissalam just said it for you. (اني) what?

00:30:52.640 --> 00:30:57.170
مُهَاجِرٌ إِلَى رَبِّ
 I'm making migration.

00:30:58.340 --> 00:31:01.550
These-- this Surah by consensus is right before Hijra.

00:31:03.240 --> 00:31:05.560
Sahaba are standing there reciting Qur'an.

00:31:05.570 --> 00:31:08.460
And they're actually reciting the game plan.

00:31:09.240 --> 00:31:10.460
This is a Makki Surah, right?

00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:13.501
What do you find at the
end of this Surah? You find:

00:31:13.525 --> 00:31:17.340
وَلا تُجَادِلُوا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ إِلاَّ بِالَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ

00:31:17.365 --> 00:31:19.800
إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا مِنْهُمْ
 Don't debate with the people

00:31:19.800 --> 00:31:21.670
of the book except with the best arguments.

00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:23.160
Wait a second.

00:31:23.740 --> 00:31:26.050
We don't debate with the people of the book in Makkah.

00:31:26.740 --> 00:31:29.350
Where is that going to happen? He's already preparing us.

00:31:30.440 --> 00:31:32.980
So what seems like an unconnected passage

00:31:32.980 --> 00:31:37.270
is actually: your trials are intense, but actually that just means migration is near.

00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:41.120
And these people's crimes have reached the point where they are

00:31:41.120 --> 00:31:43.270
now going to be dealt with the way I dealt with the

00:31:43.270 --> 00:31:45.850
nation of Nuh, the nation of Lut. They are now going to be

00:31:45.850 --> 00:31:48.460
under the 'Azaab of Allah if they don't mend their ways.

00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:49.860
So you need to get out.

00:31:50.540 --> 00:31:55.120
Very subtle and very powerful ways of getting across these kinds of messages.

00:31:55.130 --> 00:31:57.870
Things that could not have been said openly because if they said openly

00:31:57.870 --> 00:31:59.390
they would block the way to migration.

00:31:59.390 --> 00:32:01.160
You know how secretly the migration had to happen?

00:32:01.740 --> 00:32:02.160
Right?

